The YAML config now supports command sections (``scan:``, ``pull:``, ``push:``, ``parse:``) with settings that only apply to that command, and ``targets`` (``PEAT_TARGETS``) sets the scan and pull targets, so ``peat scan -c config.yaml`` works without ``-i``. The PEAT modules to use can be set with ``device_types`` in the config file or the ``PEAT_DEVICE_TYPES`` environment variable, in addition to ``-d``, and the Python API uses it when called without device types. Modules can be excluded for all targets or for specific targets (IPs, subnets, ranges, hostnames, host labels, MAC addresses, or serial ports) with ``excluded_modules``, ``PEAT_EXCLUDED_MODULES``, or the new ``-x/--exclude-modules`` argument. Exclusions from all sources are combined, and PEAT refuses to run if a module name or target in them is invalid.
